<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sidney Holland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a>–<a href="/years/1961">1961</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sir Sidney Holland</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sidney Holland was Prime Minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> from 1949 to 1957, leading the First National Government. His government abolished the Legislative Council with effect from 1951, broke the 1951 waterfront dispute with emergency regulations and signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anzus">ANZUS</a> Treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. Ill health forced his retirement in 1957.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sidney-holland.jpg" alt="Sidney Holland" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gordon Burt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sidney_George_Holland_(1953)_2.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
